================================================================================

salesforce/ja3  — https://github.com/salesforce/ja3
    Produces JA3 / JA3S fingerprints on ssl.log and JA3 Intel entries.
    License: BSD 3-Clause. Copyright (c) Salesforce.com, Inc.

netsoldier-tlsfp.zeek — first-party (deploy/docker/zeek/scripts/)
    Produces TLS client fingerprints on ssl.log in the `tls_client_fp`
    field. A clean-room implementation written from the published JA4
    TLS-client fingerprint specification, which FoxIO, LLC releases under
    BSD 3-Clause; it contains no FoxIO code. "JA4" is a trademark of
    FoxIO, LLC — netSoldier does NOT use that name for its field, type or
    branding, and references it only nominatively to state that the
    output is JA4-format compatible (for interoperability with
    JA4-labeled threat-intel feeds). The FoxIO-licensed, patent-pending
    JA4+ methods (JA4S, JA4H, JA4X, JA4L, JA4SSH, JA4T, ...) are NOT
    implemented, so no FoxIO License 1.1 obligations — including its
    restriction on monetization — apply to netSoldier.

The JA3 package runs inside the BSD-licensed Zeek process; the GPL-3.0
Go services consume only the resulting log records via ClickHouse. See
docs/adr/0003-first-party-ja4.md for the licensing analysis.

